\textbf{7. Results and Discussion}

\textbf{7.1 Final Results}

A successful run should show infrastructure containers running, the
FastAPI server lis-tening on port 8000, background consumers active,
OpenSky records entering the inges-tion pipeline, Parquet files
appearing in partitioned data-lake folders, Redis storing fast
world-state updates, and Neo4j displaying DataRecord lineage nodes. The
final evalua-tion from the project paper also shows that HVEOS improves
over a traditional static ETL baseline by using a visual DAG execution
model, background offloading, and graph-aware risk propagation. The
system was evaluated on Docker-based ARM64 nodes and demonstrated
high-throughput ingestion, low-latency updates, rapid logic
reconfigura-tion, improved AI linking accuracy, and faster graph
traversal.
\end{quote}

